# demo-store — agent context

This is a Next.js storefront. It delegates all business logic to `demo-store-api`.
Read this file before making any changes.

## Repo layout

```
app/
  (shop)/page.tsx          # Storefront UI
  api/
    auth/route.ts          # POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/sessions
    cart/route.ts          # POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/cart
    checkout/route.ts      # POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/discount + /api/mock-payment
    checkout-price/route.ts# POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/checkout-price
    edge/route.ts          # GET  — delegates to demo-store-api /api/config (Edge runtime)
    guest-orders/route.ts  # POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/guest-orders
    health/route.ts        # GET  — delegates to demo-store-api /api/ping
    orders/route.ts        # POST — delegates to demo-store-api /api/orders
    products/route.ts      # GET  — delegates to demo-store-api /api/products
    search/route.ts        # GET  — delegates to demo-store-api /api/search
lib/
  api-fetch.ts             # Shared fetch helper for calls to demo-store-api
middleware.ts              # Two-layer auth: Basic Auth (all routes) + Bearer/x-e2e-token (cron routes)
e2e/
  generate-errors.spec.ts  # Playwright script that triggers traffic across all routes
  playwright.config.ts
  package.json
```

## Auth model

middleware.ts enforces two layers on every request:

  Layer 1 — Basic Auth (all routes):
    Header: Authorization: Basic <base64(BASIC_USER:BASIC_PASS)>
    Only active if BASIC_USER and BASIC_PASS env vars are set.

  Layer 2 — E2E token (cron-only routes only):
    Header: Authorization: Bearer <E2E_TOKEN>
       OR   x-e2e-token: <E2E_TOKEN>
    Only active if E2E_TOKEN env var is set.
    Routes exempt from layer 2 (UI-safe): /api/cart, /api/auth, /api/search, /api/checkout, /api/products

The x-e2e-token header exists so browser-context fetches (which need Authorization for Basic Auth)
can still reach cron-only routes without header conflicts.

## Rules for agents working in this repo

1. All business logic lives in demo-store-api — do not add logic directly to route handlers here.
2. Route handlers in this repo should only call apiFetch and surface the response.
3. Middleware changes must preserve both auth layers and the x-e2e-token escape hatch.
4. The e2e/ directory is standalone (its own package.json) — do not add Playwright to the root package.json.
